{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794697574,"nonce":"VM30OlyGD71HmIxZaHFTjWPhLgs=","message":"OCaml plugin spike (2026-11-14, Mac, indicative until the NUC confirms).\n\nBuilt Haxe 4.3.6 from source in ~/Vibranium/haxe-src (opam, OCaml 5.1.1). Two pins needed: extlib 1.7.9 (1.8.0 made String.starts_with labelled) and mbedtls@2 via CPATH/LIBRARY_PATH (Haxe 4.3.6 targets the 2.x API); opam needs --assume-depexts because it cannot find neko.\n\nPlugin route: make plugin PLUGIN=\u003cname\u003e produces plugin.cmxs; the example plugin loads into the own build and is REJECTED by the official /usr/local/bin/haxe (symbol not found _camlLexer.get_error_pos_...), so the plugin ships with our own Haxe build.\n\ncrates/ash_tast/ocaml/ash_tast (56584dc3) reads com.types from the on_generate callback (post-DCE, no conversion to eval values): unit suite 2609 classes, 8155 function bodies, 298765 nodes, 4.4-4.7 ms. Medians over 5 interleaved reps on the Mac: typing only 2189 ms, typing + native count 2236 ms (inside the noise, range 2149-2451), Haxe exporter 4707 ms. So the macro exporter's +2.5 s is the f.expr() conversion plus eval; reading the typed AST natively costs nothing measurable. The writer is not built yet.\n\nOpen: the exporter counted 8902 functions, the plugin 8155 (definitions differ; reconcile with tast_dump before trusting either), NUC confirmation, then port the writer with tast_dump --against as the oracle.","files":null}]}